    <string name="indices">Indices</string>
    <string name="indices_intro"><![CDATA[The built-in numbers are Don Schlesinger\'s <b>Illustrious 18</b> and <b>Fab 4</b> for the Hi-Lo count, as published for a true count that is always rounded down. Deck estimate and true count rounding don\'t change them: edit any number to match your own tables. † marks a number the published sources disagree on.]]></string>
    <string name="preset">Preset</string>
    <string name="deck_estimate">Deck estimate</string>
    <string name="deck_estimate_intro"><![CDATA[How many decks count as dealt when you divide the running count by the decks left.<br><br><b>Truncate</b> counts only whole decks dealt. <b>Round</b> counts to the nearest deck. <b>95th percentile</b>, as Casino Vérité offers it, counts a deck as dealt once 50 of its cards are gone.<br><br>None of these changes an index number.]]></string>
    <string name="truncate">Truncate</string>
    <string name="round">Round</string>
    <string name="percentile_95">95th percentile</string>
    <string name="true_count_rounding">True count rounding</string>
    <string name="true_count_rounding_intro"><![CDATA[How a true count with a fraction becomes the whole number you compare with an index.<br><br><b>Floor</b> always rounds down, so −1.5 counts as −2. <b>Truncate</b> rounds toward zero, so −1.5 counts as −1. <b>Round</b> goes to the nearest whole number, a half up.<br><br>None of these changes an index number.]]></string>
    <string name="floor">Floor</string>
    <string name="flashcards">Flashcards</string>
    <string name="cards_shown">Cards shown</string>
    <string name="cards_shown_intro"><![CDATA[Choose which index each flashcard asks for.<br><br><b>%1$s</b> asks for every index switched on as often as the next.<br><br><b>%2$s</b> asks for an index more often the worse you do with it: get it right half as often and it comes up twice as often. An index you haven\'t answered yet counts as 50%% right. An index with another number, such as one you edited, starts afresh.]]></string>
